[size=6][b]✩ Handy Stylish Quick Access Wheels[/b][/size]

Two wheels of favourites for OpenMW: spells in the bottom-left corner, weapons in the bottom-right. They work alongside the vanilla quick keys, not instead of them.

[size=5][b]✩ Features[/b][/size]

The arm animations were made to be compatible with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/52596]ReAnimation v3[/url]. Without it, some visual issues might (or might not) happen.

[list]
[*][b]Hold Ready Magic[/b] (R) for the spell wheel, [b]hold Ready Weapon[/b] (F) for the weapon wheel. A short press still readies or puts away as usual.
[*][b]Point with the mouse, let go to equip.[/b] Time slows down while a wheel is open.
[*][b]Ready Magic / Ready Weapon + Quick Menu[/b] (F1), in either order, adds your current spell or weapon to its wheel. Do it again to take it off.
[*][b]Hold the right mouse button and move the mouse[/b] to move a slot to reorganise the order, [b]double right click[/b] to remove it.
[*]Items you no longer carry and spells you no longer know are taken off the wheels on their own (each can be turned off in the settings).
[*]The arm on the wheel's side comes up: its fingertips glow with the pointed spell's magic, and the pointed weapon is drawn for a look.
[*]With [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/55327]Dynamic Camera[/url] installed, the background is blurred.
[*]Follows whatever keys you have bound. A short tutorial shows the first time; the rest is in Options -> Scripts -> Stylish Quick Access Wheels.
[/list]

[size=5][b]✩ How to install[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Requires OpenMW 0.51 or newer.[/b]
[*]Install this mod [b]with a mod organiser[/b]: download the archive (or this repository as an archive) and drag and drop it into your mod organiser of choice (e.g [url=https://github.com/ModOrganizer2/modorganizer/releases]Mod Organizer 2[/url] on Windows or [url=https://github.com/grazelandsnomad/nerevarine_organizer/releases/tag/v0.70]Nerevarine Organizer[/url] on Linux). [b]Or[/b] [url=https://modding-openmw.com/tips/installing-mods/]read this tutorial[/url] on how to install mods using the launcher or completely manually (it's also very easy).
[*]Enable [font=Courier New]QuickAccessWheel.omwscripts[/font] in the "Content Files" tab of the OpenMW launcher.
[/list]

Have fun!

